      "research_entry": "The last authenticated claim expired 16:43:28Z on November 18. Its prior scientific checkpoint already states, subject to its two named antecedents, that the elementary null-lattice quotient for q=3^a is (Z/3)^(4q-8); constructive generators/normal form, a distinct all-horizon content question, and signed native triadic legality were still open. Later public author drafts supplied explicit minimal generators (#2717), the all-q all-horizon contents for q>=9 (#2734), all-trit short-horizon Frobenius discrepancy (#2749), and the conditional exact mod-9 eventual period 54 and preperiod 9 at q=9 (#2752). These distinct later scientific findings are unmerged and marked not independently reviewed. Another author draft (#2753) also covers the q=9 mod-27/81 periods. The present selection studies fast retrieval of the coefficients of the existing EJ basis, rather than constructing the basis or repeating a known residue period. The positive terminal observer and algebraic branch do not supply native signed-rotation authorization.",
